          "english_quote": "the service they had received to perform",
          "issue": "The translation follows the selected working reading, but its notes do not disclose the editorial supplement. The supplied apparatus reports “xxvi. 2 διακονῆσαι] supp. Gebhardt.” The general working-text statement does not distinguish this supplemented wording from preserved text.",
          "suggested_revision": "Retain the working translation, subject to fresh review, and add a source note explaining that the supplied apparatus attributes διακονῆσαι (“to perform/serve”) to Gebhardt’s supplement. Identify this as an edition-reported editorial supplement, not newly verified manuscript wording.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ τὰ θηρία ἃ εἶδες εἰς τὸ ὄρος οὗτοί εἰσιν.",
          "english_quote": "They are the wild beasts you saw on the mountain.",
          "issue": "The main text accurately follows the selected reading, but no note discloses the supplied apparatus alternative at this clause: A reportedly prefixes θʹ, meaning “ninth,” whereas L₁ and L₂ support the unqualified mountain wording; E is reported deficient. The opening reference to the ninth mountain does not disclose this local textual difference.",
          "suggested_revision": "Keep “the mountain” in the main text and add a note stating that the supplied edition-apparatus transcription reports A as reading “the ninth mountain,” L₁ and L₂ as supporting the selected wording, and E as deficient here. Attribute these reports without claiming fresh witness verification.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
