      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ἧς ἔλαβον διακονῆ⸢σαι⸣",
          "english_quote": "They used the service entrusted to them to enrich themselves.",
          "issue": "This sentence reasonably compresses the selected service clause, but the simplified edition independently lacks disclosure of its supplemented source wording. The supplied apparatus attributes διακονῆσαι to Gebhardt’s supplement; neither the footnotes nor metadata distinguishes that editorial contribution from preserved text.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source note explaining that the printed working reading includes διακονῆσαι (“to perform/serve”), attributed by the supplied apparatus to Gebhardt’s supplement. Retain the distinction between an editorial supplement and manuscript wording; any revised sentence or note requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ τὰ θηρία ἃ εἶδες εἰς τὸ ὄρος οὗτοί εἰσιν.",
          "english_quote": "They are the wild beasts you saw on the mountain.",
          "issue": "The simplified text follows the selected source, but its notes omit the supplied local alternative “the ninth mountain,” reportedly represented by A’s prefixed θʹ. Its metadata claim to retain “all textual alternatives” is therefore not fulfilled for this unit.",
          "suggested_revision": "Retain the selected main-text wording and add an accessible note reporting the A alternative, the L₁/L₂ support for the working reading, and the reported deficiency of E. Describe these as supplied apparatus reports, not independently authenticated readings.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions were reviewed independently against all eight source paragraphs. Their English covers the clauses and preserves the conditional judgments, uncertainty, impossibility statement, negations, and policy-compliant servant and repentance terminology. Both require source-note revisions to distinguish an editorial supplement and disclose the reported local mountain alternative. These findings do not require replacing the selected working readings. Proposed corrections require fresh review; this assessment does not authenticate unseen manuscripts or certify exhaustive collation."
